---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
import '../styles/legal.css';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Strictons collects, uses, stores and protects personal information, and how to contact us about privacy."
>
  <article class="legal-page">
    <header class="legal-hero">
      <div class="legal-shell">
        <p class="legal-kicker">Privacy</p>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="legal-intro">
          This policy explains how Strictons handles personal information when
          you visit our website, contact us or work with us.
        </p>
        <p class="legal-updated">Last updated 24 September 2026</p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="legal-shell legal-content">
      <section>
        <h2>About this policy</h2>
        <p>
          Strictons is based in New South Wales, Australia. We respect your
          privacy and aim to handle personal information in line with the
          Privacy Act 1988 (Cth) and the Australian Privacy Principles where
          they apply to us.
        </p>
        <p>
          In this policy, “personal information” means information or an opinion
          about an identified individual, or an individual who is reasonably
          identifiable.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Information we collect</h2>
        <p>Depending on how you interact with us, we may collect:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>your name, work contact details, job title and organisation;</li>
          <li>
            information you include in an enquiry, meeting booking, email or
            other communication;
          </li>
          <li>
            information needed to plan, create, produce and maintain a guide,
            including hotel or business details, brand assets and approvals;
          </li>
          <li>
            technical information sent by your browser or device, such as your
            IP address, device type, browser type, pages visited and access
            times; and
          </li>
          <li>any other information you choose to give us.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We do not generally seek sensitive information. Please do not send it
          unless it is reasonably necessary and we have agreed to receive it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>How we collect information</h2>
        <p>
          We usually collect information directly from you when you email, call,
          book a meeting, make an enquiry or work with us. We may also receive
          business contact information from your organisation, a referral, a
          publicly available source or a service provider acting on our behalf.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our website does not currently use advertising or analytics cookies.
          If you use the booking calendar on our Contact page, Cal.com may set
          cookies or collect information under its own privacy terms. You can
          contact us by email instead if you prefer not to use the calendar.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Why we use personal information</h2>
        <p>We may use personal information to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>respond to enquiries and arrange meetings;</li>
          <li>provide, manage and improve our guides and related services;</li>
          <li>
            communicate with hotels, local businesses, suppliers and other
            people we work with;
          </li>
          <li>send service messages and agreed marketing communications;</li>
          <li>operate, secure and improve our website;</li>
          <li>manage our records, accounts and business operations; and</li>
          <li>comply with legal obligations and resolve disputes.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          You may unsubscribe from marketing emails at any time by using the
          unsubscribe option in the message or emailing us.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>When we share information</h2>
        <p>
          We may disclose personal information to people who need it to support
          our work, including hosting, email, scheduling, design, printing,
          professional advisory and technology providers. We may also disclose
          information where you have asked or authorised us to, where required
          by law, or in connection with a business restructure or transfer.
        </p>
        <p>
          Some providers may store or process information outside Australia. The
          countries involved can change as providers update their systems.
          Contact us if you would like current details relevant to your
          information.
        </p>
        <p>We do not sell personal information.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Storage and security</h2>
        <p>
          We may hold information electronically and, where necessary, in
          physical records. We take reasonable steps to protect it from misuse,
          interference, loss and unauthorised access, modification or
          disclosure. No method of storage or transmission is completely secure,
          so we cannot guarantee absolute security.
        </p>
        <p>
          We keep personal information only for as long as reasonably needed for
          the purpose for which it was collected, our business records and any
          legal obligations. We then delete, destroy or de-identify it where
          appropriate.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Access, correction and complaints</h2>
        <p>
          You may ask to access personal information we hold about you or ask us
          to correct it. You may also contact us with a privacy question or
          complaint. Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> and describe
          your request. We may need to verify your identity before responding.
        </p>
        <p>
          We will respond within a reasonable time. If you are not satisfied
          with our response and the Privacy Act applies, you may contact the
          Office of the Australian Information Commissioner at <a
            href="https://www.oaic.gov.au"
            rel="external">oaic.gov.au</a
          >.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this policy when our practices or legal obligations
          change. The current version will be published here with its effective
          date.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
